    {
      "id": "9f882775-07c9-497e-a403-39481d40c45e",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -1232
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1224,
        "height": 1340,
        "content": "## Monitor LinkedIn posts from target accounts with Periodix Actions, Claude, and Slack\n\nWatch the people and companies you sell to and get a Slack alert every time one of them posts on LinkedIn, with a one-line summary, why it matters for you, a comment idea, and a message opener that references the post. Never miss the moment a target account talks about a new priority, a hire, a launch, or a problem you solve.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every morning, reads your target accounts (people or company pages) from the Accounts tab.\n2. The first time it sees an account, it resolves the LinkedIn author ID and saves it back to the sheet, so later runs skip this step.\n3. Periodix Actions fetches each account's latest posts.\n4. Only new posts are kept: already-seen posts, reposts, and posts older than your window are skipped.\n5. Claude summarizes each post, rates its relevance to what you sell, and drafts a comment idea and a message opener.\n6. Each new post is saved to the Posts tab and sent to Slack.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified Periodix Actions node (works on n8n Cloud and self-hosted), sign up at actions.periodix.net, connect a LinkedIn profile, and pick it in the three Periodix Actions nodes.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with two tabs: Accounts (columns: account_name, linkedin_url, author_id; leave author_id empty) and Posts (columns: post_id, social_id, account_name, linkedin_url, post_url, posted_at, text, reactions, comments, reposts, summary, relevance, why, comment_angle, dm_opener, slack_text, found_at).\n3. Connect Google Sheets, Slack, and your Anthropic credential, set your Sheet ID and Slack channel, and describe what you sell in Monitor Config.\n\n### Limits\nOne connected LinkedIn profile can monitor up to 100 accounts per day (Get User Posts allows 100 requests per account per day). Resolving people uses Get Profile, about 100 per day, once per account. For bigger lists, connect more profiles and split the Accounts tab.\n\n### Customization\nSwap Slack for Gmail, Microsoft Teams, or a CRM task. Only alert on posts with relevance 7 or higher by adding a filter before Slack. Feed social_id into Get Post Reactions or Get Post Comments to pull everyone engaging with a target account's post.\n\n### Why not an Apify post scraper\nNo cookies to refresh, no proxies, no actor rental or per-run fees. One node resolves IDs, pulls posts, and later handles reactions, comments, connection requests, and messages.\n\n### Pricing\n$10/month per connected LinkedIn profile with 1,000 results included, and every next 2,000 results for just $10, or $49/month unlimited.\n\nBuilt on the infrastructure behind Periodix (rated 4.9/5 on G2): 0 LinkedIn accounts lost across 25,000 connected profiles in the last 24 months."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
